I did verify to dump EEPROM data and also write EEPROM by per byte.

1.Plug dm9601/dm9621 adapter and has get dm9601.ko be 'insmod' to have =
'eht0',
2.Run ethtool v3.7 (as attached executable file and it's help display.)
3. Commands:
   ./ethtool -e eth0  (dump EEPROM data for all the .get_eeprom_len )
   ./ethtool -E eth0 magic 0x9620 offset 0 value 0xf1  (write 0xf1 to =
eeprom byte0)
   ./ethtool -E eth0 magic 0x9620 offset 1 value 0xf2  (write 0xf2 to =
eeprom byte1)
   ./ethtool -E eth0 magic 0x9620 offset 2 value 0xf3  (write 0xf3 to =
eeprom byte2)

*I am not sure if it can cover all the huge purpose functions of =
ethtool, or
 some leakage in such implementation. Thanks and need further advice~

